   "date": "2014-09-02T18:31:59Z",
   "subject": "Testing Assumptions for Mediationanalysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there!<div><br></div><div>Does anybody know if it is possible to test several assumptions (e.g. homoscedasticy, multikollinearity, normal distribution of residuals)</div><div>within a mediation model (with more than 1 mediator)?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you so much for your advice!</div><div><br></div><div>Laura</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xySDFmlGAFMJ",
   "from": "Sunthud Pornprasertmanit",
   "author": "af82fa98896529e2",
   "date": "2014-09-02T18:56:36Z",
   "subject": "Re: Testing Assumptions for Mediationanalysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is a good question. I am not sure I have a good answer on this. One way to check the assumptions is to find the factor scores of latent variables and check the assumptions on the factor scores like multiple regressions. Here is the example code:<div>\r\n<br></div><div><div>library(lavaan)</div><div>mod2 &lt;- &#39; X  =~ x1 + x2 + x3</div><div>              M =~ x4 + x5 + x6</div><div>              Y   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 </div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t</span>  Y ~ c*X + b*M</div>\r\n<div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t</span>M ~ a*X</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t</span>ab := a*b</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t</span>total := c + (a*b)</div><div>&#39;</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>fit2 &lt;- sem(mod2, data=HolzingerSwineford1939)</div><div><br></div><div>summary(fit2, fit.measures=TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>fscores &lt;- predict(fit2)</div><div>fscores &lt;- as.data.frame(fscores)</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>library(psych)</div><div>describe(fscores)</div><div><br></div><div>predM &lt;- coef(fit2)[&quot;a&quot;] * fscores$X</div><div>predY &lt;- coef(fit2)[&quot;c&quot;] * fscores$X + coef(fit2)[&quot;b&quot;] * fscores$M</div>\r\n<div>residM &lt;- fscores$M - predM</div><div>residY &lt;- fscores$Y - predY</div><div><br></div><div># Residual plot to check the heteroscadasticity</div><div>plot(predM, residM)</div><div>plot(predY, residY)</div><div><br>\r\n</div><div># Check the skewness and kurtosis of residuals</div><div>describe(cbind(residM, residY))</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>For the multicollinearity, you can just run CFA and see the factor correlations of predictors. To check the tolerance, you can predict one predictors by other predictors and investigate R-square (i.e., 1 - tolerance).</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Sep 2, 2014 at 1:31 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">laura.m...@googlemail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there!<div><br></div><div>Does anybody know if it is possible to test several assumptions (e.g. homoscedasticy, multikollinearity, normal distribution of residuals)</div>\r\n<div>within a mediation model (with more than 1 mediator)?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you so much for your advice!</div><div><br></div><div>Laura</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div><div><br>\r\n</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431232825000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kPmH9TMq9JF_yT_UM4j9Q\">http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431232826000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1z0ixitAzqwoCnCjd7I_Rp\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
